{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792611723,"nonce":"/2QW27fncqPpJ3ENQJWcQ9OguTI=","title":"`release_gate_external` (crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs ~6652-6681) releases an `external` gate after verifying HMAC(secret, \"{run}:{step}\") and never calls the Environment's `admits()`. An `external` gate inside a Deploy Run into a protected Environment is therefore released by the HMAC alone — approvers, wait timer and allowed refs of that Environment are not consulted at that point.","message":"Decide whether an external gate in a protected Environment must also satisfy the Environment's rules (approvers accumulated, wait timer elapsed) before release, or document that an external gate is an explicit author-chosen bypass (and then reconcile with the approvals-opt-in ticket).\nAcceptance: behaviour decided and tested; a Deploy Run into an Environment with approvers cannot be released past its approvals by an external-gate HMAC alone (if that is the decision).\nFound by the 2026-10-22 deployments/plugins design audit (independent judge), verified by hand.","files":null}]}